          "filename": "Corgarff Castle, Strathdon (20miles north of Braemar) - geograph.org.uk - 463640.jpg",
          "caption": "Corgarff Castle, Strathdon (20miles north of Braemar) I took this photograph as we started a 6 hour walk around the nearby Brown Cow Hill which is a \"Corbett\" i.e. between 2500 and 3000 feet.\nThe Castle sits high above the start of the difficult Cockbridge to Tomintoul Road ( The Lecht).\nThe infant river Don flows eastwards on its north side emerging high on the nearby hills.\n\nThe castle is a visitor attraction which belongs to Historic Scotland and has recently been given a makeover.",
